    "summary": "Alligator monster, Dark Star > St Stephen > The Eleven brilliance",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a towering Alligator jam and a historic Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven sequence. Garcia’s tube‑warm guitar soars while Phil’s bass drives the psychedelic interplay. Recommended for anyone hunting definitive mid‑’68 performances.",
    "review": "On August 21, 1968 at the Fillmore West the Dead turned the venue into a laboratory of fire‑breathing improvisation. The first set rolls through the Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One suite before erupting into an Alligator marathon that climbs through a second drum break and a wild jam, showcasing Garcia’s “on‑fire” tone and Pigpen’s gritty organ on Good Morning Little School Girl. The second set is where legend is made: Dark Star unfurls into Saint Stephen and then into the vocal‑led Eleven, a sequence praised as the first of its kind, with Lesh’s bass weaving a psychic dance around Garcia’s lead. The night closes with a searing Turn On Your Lovelight and a soulful In The Midnight Hour encore. Across all four soundboard sources the playing is consistently high‑energy and tight; the recommended Cotsman SBD captures the crystal‑clear guitar, balanced organ, and crisp drums while avoiding the minor tape hiss and edit quirks of other versions.",
